    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-045: Inline Background Images**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~300 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Honest framing: zero first-viewport delta.** All `.external` targets are in article body content, not page chrome. Verifiable only after scrolling ~4-5 viewport heights to the first external link.\n\n## Measurement (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-29)\n\n### The decisive breakdown\n\n| Category | Count | Renders via ADR-045? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `background-size` on **`mask-image`** targets | **13** | No — mask-image is separate subsystem |\n| `background-size` on **`background-image`** target | **1** | ✅ Yes — the only renderable rule |\n| `background-position: center` (mask targets) | 13 | No |\n| `background-position: center -16px` (hover) | 1 | No |\n| `background-position: center right` | 1 | ✅ Yes (a.external) |\n| `background-repeat: no-repeat` | 15 | All targets |\n\n**Only 1 rule (`.mw-parser-output a.external`) uses `background-image` + size/position/repeat.** The other 13 size rules target `mask-image` (a different CSS subsystem, not implemented).\n\n### The 1 renderable rule\n\n```css\n.mw-parser-output a.external {\n    background-image: url(...link-external-small-ltr-progressive.svg);\n    background-position: center right;\n    background-repeat: no-repeat;\n    background-size: 0.857em;\n    padding-right: 1em;\n}\n```\n\n**242 `.external` elements in article HTML.** First at char 108015 (History section, ~3000 words in).\n\n## Scope\n\n### Commit 1 (parse + fragment fields, behavior-neutral)\n- `LineFragment` gains 6 background fields + 2 position keyword enums\n- `background-size` (fixed length; `auto` default), `background-position` (keyword pairs), `background-repeat` (no-repeat only)\n- Fragment production populates fields from `ComputedStyleMap`\n- **Inline padding**: diagnostic-first. If `flatten_inline_to_words` doesn't honor `padding-right`, extend it (icon placement depends on it)\n- Zero paint changes\n\n### Commit 2 (paint, scroll-verified)\n- New `paint_inline_image()` helper\n- `InlineContext` case in `paint_children` draws backgrounds before glyphs\n- **Position keywords resolve in paint** (against loaded icon dimensions — avoids layout-time image loading)\n- **Scroll-position PNG verification**: BEFORE / AFTER at first `.external` link (~4-5 scroll heights down)\n- Regression checks: block backgrounds (034), title underline (042), toolbar line (043), issue box (040)\n\n### Commit 3 (docs)\n- ADR-045 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-045 note in ADR-034 (inline extension)\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- **`mask-image`** (13 of 14 `background-size` rules in Wikipedia CSS) — separate subsystem, own ADR\n- `background-size: cover | contain` (0 uses)\n- Percentage `background-size` / `background-position` (0 uses)\n- `background-repeat: repeat | repeat-x | repeat-y` (0 uses)\n- Multi-layer backgrounds (0 uses)\n- `background-clip` / `background-origin` (0 uses)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Zero first-viewport delta is honestly framed** — the delta is real (242 icons next to external links) but only visible after scrolling into article body. This is analogous to ADR-044's \"visually subtle\" caveat — the delta exists but not where first-viewport PNG would catch it. Scroll-position PNG is equivalent rigor for article-body targets. Agree?\n- [ ] **Per-fragment fields (not box-level)** — inline elements become `LineFragment`s (flattened from `LayoutInline`), no box to attach to. Per-fragment fields mirror ADR-018's per-fragment `element` pointer. Agree?\n- [ ] **Keyword position (not raw px)** — layout can't compute `x_px = frag.width - icon_width` without loading the image (layout/paint feedback loop). Store keywords (`Right` + `Center`); resolve in paint against loaded dimensions. Agree?\n- [ ] **`mask-image` deferred** — 13 of 14 size rules target mask-image, a separate CSS subsystem. Would be a separate ADR. Agree?\n- [ ] **Inline padding may extend Commit 1 scope** — if `flatten_inline_to_words` doesn't currently honor `padding-right`, extending it is a documented scope addition in Commit 1's message. Not pre-confirmed; diagnostic first.\n- [ ] **Scroll-position PNG verification** — verify at ~4-5 scroll heights down where first `.external` appears. Not first-viewport.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 562 / 2188 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/045-inline-backgrounds.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #217\n",
